From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:31:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): show synchronization in the system tray

Motivation: on KDE Plasma and other desktops with a StatusNotifierItem host
there is no way back to a hidden window and no sign that DriveSync keeps
running; the Background portal does not provide either for a program
installed from a distribution package.

Changes: a StatusNotifierItem (org.kde.StatusNotifierItem with a
com.canonical.dbusmenu menu: Open DriveSync, Quit) is exported on the
session bus with GIO and registered with org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher when
one is present. Its icon, overlay, status and tooltip follow each account's
public synchronization status (idle, working, conflict, needs a decision,
failed), read through monitor_synchronization; retryable waits stay
"working". While a tray host shows the item, closing the window hides it
there and posts the existing "continues running" notice; without a host the
Background portal path is unchanged. No new dependency.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets
-D warnings, unit tests for the status classification and for the menu's
D-Bus types; in a Plasma 6.7 session the watcher lists the item and the
system tray shows it, its menu's Open DriveSync shows the window, a closed
window keeps DriveSync running in the tray and comes back from it. The
unchanged build registers no item.

Limitations: no real Google account was used; the tray was checked on
Plasma only.

